  <NAME>RNA-seq data of effects of DCPS inhibition in mouse AML cells (CALM/AF10) and in normal GMP cells. Overall mRNA profiles of CALM/AF10 (#1/#2) and MLL/AF9 (#1/#2).</NAME>
  <TITLE>RNA-seq data of effects of DCPS inhibition in mouse AML cells (CALM/AF10) and in normal GMP cells. Overall mRNA profiles of CALM/AF10 (#1/#2) and MLL/AF9 (#1/#2).</TITLE>
  <DESCRIPTION>Purpose: The goals of this study are to assess the possibility whether DCPS inhibition would impair pre-mRNA splicing in AML cells/normal GMP, and to assess overall effects of DCPS inhibition. Overall design: Methods: mRNA profiles of AML (CALM/AF10) and normal GMP cells at 0h, 6h and 10h after RG3039 treatment were generated by deep sequencing, in triplicate, using NextSeq. RNA-seq data were analyzed using a bioinformatic pipeline enabling quantification of exon-exon junctions without predetermining alternative aplicing models of annotating splice junctions as described (Darman et al., 2015). Methods: RNA-seq experiments were performed using 4 indicated AML lines.</DESCRIPTION>
